[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2425297014","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98346#issuecomment-2425297014","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98346","id":2425297014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Qjxh2","user":{"login":"RedMser","id":5117197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTcxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5117197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser","html_url":"https://github.com/RedMser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-20T23:48:41Z","updated_at":"2024-10-20T23:48:41Z","body":"You need to update the Texture2D.xml file to include documentation for the method, see: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/contributing/documentation/updating_the_class_reference.html#updating-class-reference-when-working-on-the-engine\r\n\r\nIf you don't have a way to easily compile the engine, you can instead apply the diff in the failing check as a basis: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/11420093268/job/31775421526?pr=98346","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2425297014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2517809223","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98346#issuecomment-2517809223","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98346","id":2517809223,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WErhH","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-04T15:39:05Z","updated_at":"2024-12-04T15:57:22Z","body":"Edit: OK, I looked through the source again to resolve my confusion with these functions.\r\n\r\nIt seems `_is_pixel_opaque` is already exposed through `Texture2D`. \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/25dd96179ca38da52762000594c35ec30b22a5da/scene/resources/texture.cpp#L113\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/25dd96179ca38da52762000594c35ec30b22a5da/doc/classes/Texture2D.xml#L69-L76\r\n\r\n`is_pixel_opaque` is a c++ virtual function that, by default, calls its `GDVirtual` implementation:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/25dd96179ca38da52762000594c35ec30b22a5da/scene/resources/texture.cpp#L51-L55\r\n\r\nThough in the case of `ImageTexture` it is overriden in c++ land:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/scene/resources/image_texture.cpp#L176-L207\r\n\r\nI guess your fix of exposing the static function is therefore appropriate.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2517809223/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589524273","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98346#issuecomment-2589524273","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98346","id":2589524273,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aWQEx","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T10:17:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T10:17:53Z","body":"Could you amend the commit message to be more explicit? Like this PR's title would be a better option, as it clarifies which class we're talking about.\r\nI'd normally do such edits myself but it seems maintainer pushes on this PR are disabled.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589524273/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589556927","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98346#issuecomment-2589556927","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98346","id":2589556927,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aWYC_","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T10:32:24Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T10:32:24Z","body":"I looked at what is_pixel_opaque does in the code and it seems a bit more complex than just a check against alpha. I'm concerned we're exposing something somewhat internal here. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589556927/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589582594","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98346#issuecomment-2589582594","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98346","id":2589582594,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aWeUC","user":{"login":"SourceOfHTML","id":70210240,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjEwMjQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70210240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML","html_url":"https://github.com/SourceOfHTML","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T10:44:58Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T10:44:58Z","body":"If it were entirely internal, surely we wouldn't list it in documentation, then? We could remove it from documentation too\r\n\r\nAlternatively, if we're really worried about over-exposing, we could just re-write it from scratch, maybe?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2589582594/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"perform